    reasoning: 'The LIB holds protocol mappings and can contain more state than the active forwarding plane needs. A usable outgoing label must correspond to a valid downstream receiving context on a selected or specifically programmed alternate path.',
    example: 'At PE1, P2’s remote label can remain while the primary route uses P1. After the P1–P2 failure, PE1 can install two cost-51 OSPF next hops if supported, each with its own qualified rewrite.',
